    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d329">

                <pb facs="0351" n="345" xml:id="pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123M956/386: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers (Cole) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-26T00:00:00+01:00">July 26,
                            1942—midnight.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 27—10:41 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>490. From Murphy. Your 220, July 24, 9 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">p.m.</hi>] I
                    do not foresee any difficulty returning to North Africa. I hold visas for the
                    three French North African territories good until February 1943 and no visa is
                    required for the Tangier Zone. [Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cole</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
